SUMMARY:Pay what you can event Dance and Motion Signature Series Event
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## Tickets for the event are av
 ailable only on WTPG.NGO\n\n## Details\n\n\\#\\# Tickets for the event are
  available only on WTPG\\.NGO\nHere si the link to buy a ticket to the eve
 nt -[https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/pay-what-you-can-event-dance-and-m
 otion-signature-series-event-2](https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/pay-wha
 t-you-can-event-dance-and-motion-signature-series-event-2)\n\\#\\# About t
 he event\nOur pay what you can events are designed to reduce the existing 
 financial participation barriers and allow everyone in the community to en
 joy photography. We have partnered with Exhibition Place Park for this ser
 ies of fun and very unique workshops. We have been serving the arts commun
 ity since 2011 and we are very aware of the financial limitations of some 
 of our 9000 members. If you can pay more to help support us please do\, if
  you you cant please give what you can and if the fee is not feasible for 
 you please email Phil Sutherland at [[phil@wtpg.ngo](http://phil@wtpg.ngo/
 )]([mailto:phil@wtpg.ngo](http://mailto:phil@wtpg.ngo/)) and he can help a
 ssist if you can not afford to purchase a ticket at all.\n6:30-9:30 pm eve
 nt at Exhibition Place Park on the Bandshell Page\nInstructor - Phil Suthe
 rland - Elinchrom Brand Ambassador\nWe will have some great gear from Elin
 chrom at the event for everyone to use on July 3rd\nWe are thrilled to ann
 ounce our upcoming Outdoor location Lighting Workshop at the world famous 
 CNE Bandshell stage that has hosted legendary performances by Louis Armstr
 ong \,Glen Campbell\, Blondie\, Bob Hope\,Quincy Jones\, The Monowhales\, 
 Big Wreck\, Frankie Avalon\, Susan Aglukark\, The Beach Boys and hundreds 
 of more performers over the last 90 years. The CNE Bandstand design is ins
 pired by theHollywood Bowl\, the Art Deco-styled shell was built in 1936 a
 ccording to designs prepared by the Toronto architectural firm of Craig an
 d Madill.\n**Workshop Details:** With the talented model Julia we will cre
 ate beautiful images of a Dancer in Motion and use some really cool gear f
 rom Elinchrom to light the stage during the shoot. Join us for this exciti
 ng opportunity to explore studio lighting setups on location and a world f
 amous venue and create dramatic images to enhance your photography portfol
 io while learning some cool techniques.\n**Workshop Details:** Do you aspi
 re to learn the secrets of beautiful and creative lighting techniques? We 
 are dedicated to lighting and sharing our photographic knowledge with you.
  Our fun group lighting workshop with professional instructors is designed
  to cater to your interests as an artist and creator of any skill level in
  a fun and engaging community arts workshop. Throughout the workshop\, we 
 will discuss the specific lighting setups for each scenario\, explaining t
 he choice of modifiers and angles to effectively illuminate the subject an
 d accessories and individually all get a chance to get hands on time with 
 the Elinchrom gear and shoot the model.\n**Instructor:** Phil Sutherland -
  Elinchrom Brand Ambassador\n**Assistant:** Reanna Niceforo\n**Model:** Th
 e exceptionally talented Julia Walton. Her remarkable dance skills will co
 ntribute to creating stunning images during the workshop.\nAs an indigenou
 s-run\, not-for-profit arts group\, we are dedicated to serving the whole 
 artistic community and advocating for the photographic arts. At our core\,
  we believe in sharing knowledge and the joy of photography with the commu
 nity. We strive to make art accessible to everyone and work hard to bring 
 arts programming to the community. We can not wait to spend some quality t
 ime creating art with you!\n**Workshop Details:**\n\n* Workshop Fee: Pay w
 hat you can (if this was a usual paid event in Toronto it would be $85-325
  per participant we set the min at $5) We are opening up the price as pay 
 what you can in an effort to ensure everyone who wants to attend can. If y
 ou can not afford any payment please email Phil Sutherland to get added to
  the guest list for the event [[phil@wtpg.ngo](http://phil@wtpg.ngo/)]([ma
 ilto:phil@wtpg.ngo](http://mailto:phil@wtpg.ngo/))\n*\n\n**Items to Bring:
 **\n\n* Camera/Lenses of choice (DSLR\, medium format\, or mirrorless)\n* 
 Fully charged battery\n* Freshly formatted memory card(s)\n* General lense
 s\n* Pen and paper (if you wish to take notes)\n\nSo that you know\, tripo
 ds or camera supports are recommended for this workshop but are not necess
 ary to participate.\n**Triggers:** We provide wireless triggers for most m
 ainstream camera types. Our trigger works with any standard camera hot sho
 e\n**Model Release:** A West Toronto Photography Group model release form\
 , will be provided to each participant for non-commercial use and training
  purposes. The model will sign these forms\, and printed copies will be pr
 ovided to each photographer.\n**Cancellation Policy:** Refunds will be iss
 ued within 72 hours if we\, as organizers\, have to postpone or cancel the
  event. We understand that sometimes circumstances prevent attendance at a
  workshop. If you cannot attend\, please get in touch with us as soon as p
 ossible\, and we will help you resell your workshop spot to the group. We 
 will reimburse you for the ticket price if we can resell the ticket. Howev
 er\, if we cannot resell the spot\, you may transfer it to someone else to
  attend in your place\, but unfortunately\, no refund will be provided.\nW
 e look forward to welcoming you to this inspiring workshop and helping you
  enhance your photography skills
